# Write & manage code

## Write
- One module = one reason to change. Prefer composition over inheritance.
- Name by domain role (`FeatureRow`), not tech accident (`Helper2`).
- Pure logic at the core; I/O, UI, and frameworks at the edges.
- Explicit inputs/outputs; no hidden globals; fail loud with typed/clear errors.
- Match local style (imports, components, CSS modules). Duplicate patterns over inventing new abstractions.

## Manage
- Keep folders by feature/section when the app is UI-led; share only true primitives in `ui/` / `lib/`.
- Public surface small: export barrels only for stable APIs.
- Delete dead code; avoid commented-out graves and speculative “for later” hooks.
- Refactor only behind green behavior (tests or manual checklist), in small commits of intent.

## Reject
- God components, prop drilling through 4+ layers without a local seam, premature micro-libs, config sprawl.
